source: crates/cyberspine-asm/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
Assemble a .csa source into a .csp image

Usage: cyinea [OPTIONS] --asm-file <ASM_FILE>

Options:
  -a, --asm-file <ASM_FILE>
          The `.csa` source file to assemble

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Where to write the assembled `.csp`. Defaults to the input with a `.csp` extension

  -r, --rig <RIG>
          The rig manifest to assemble for; overrides the source's `.rig`. A relative path is resolved against the `.csa`'s own directory

      --deny-warnings
          Treat readability warnings as errors

      --json
          Emit diagnostics as JSON Lines on stdout instead of a terminal rendering on stderr. One stream, one record per line (`docs/diagnostics.md`)

      --strip
          Strip the debug segment: produce a release build (`docs/asm.md` §8).
          
          Without this flag the image carries a `pc → source position` table and a label table (`docs/binfmt.md` §6.7); execution is identical either way.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
